{"id":"_summary","shard":"Jewelry-03","checked":300,"ok":219,"issues":81,"by_kind":{"category":33,"variant":25,"facets":15,"name":9,"duplicate":5,"brand":1},"high":16,"rule_gaps":["'kjede' in a name still resolves to Jewelry even when the leaf crumb is clearly another department (Boksing/Tilbehør Boksesekk → Sport, Gardinskinner → Home) or there is no crumb at all (KMC bike chain from Bikeshop → Bikes)","a 'Ringer'/'ringer' crumb under Jakt > Optikk (riflescope rings/mounts) resolves to Jewelry — needs a Jakt/Optikk guard, 3 Warne rows here","'Knapper'/'Metallspenne' under 'Sy og Strikk' and Panduro's 'Grunnmaterialer' (bead/finding craft supplies) resolve to Jewelry instead of Hobby","metal-colour words alone ('gull', 'Sølv', 'Silver') promote non-jewellery rows into Jewelry: a curtain bracket, a wall hook, an XLR connector, a mop cloth","'Charms' in a book title matched the jewellery vocabulary and the crumb 'Manga' is unmapped → a manga volume sits in Jewelry","silver flatware sold by jewellers (spisekniv, gaffel, skje, paispade, koldtgaffel) has no rule and lands in Jewelry instead of Kitchen — 8 rows here, all from Mestergull's contentless 'Produkter' breadcrumb","facetrules stone: pearl compounds (Akoyaperle, Tahitiperler) and gemstone names (granat, røkkvarts, aventurin) are missed, while the separate words 'perler'/'topas' hit","facetrules type: 'diamantring'/'alliansering' and the crumbs Diamantringer/Allianseringer do not derive type=Rings (only a bare 'Ringer' crumb does)"],"notes":"Core jewellery (David-Andersen, Mestergull, Bjørklund, Sylvsmidja bunadsølv) is in good shape; nearly all damage is at the edges — 33 rows are not jewellery at all, most of them dragged in by a metal-colour word or the word 'kjede'/'ringer'. Two structural weaknesses beyond the rules: Mockberg is listed twice (Bjørklund slug rows vs Klokker.no EAN rows) so colour/size siblings and two exact duplicates sit as separate top-level rows with no variant wiring, and 133 of 300 rows have no image because these shops are only sampled. Mestergull's crawl also yields near-useless names ('Kjede Sølv' x8, 'KLONDIKE 0,14 ct.') and 'Produkter' as the whole breadcrumb, which is why its rows are the worst-classified in the shard."}
